/**
 * Base type for a spec parameter of a method. Such parameters are helpful for specifying complex options to methods
 * and for defining and documenting default values. Spec objects have additional validation when passed as
 * arguments, see {@link ValidateObjSpec}.
 *
 * Spec-specific validation requires all mandatory fields to have values. If an object embedded within a spec
 * object is also a spec, it is also verified. This allows the implementer of a method that takes a spec to know
 * that the spec will be "complete".
 *
 * ```type
 * type OperationSpec mixes Spec {
 *   scalpel: !int = 10
 * }
 * ```
 *
 * Implementation of a method which takes **OperationSpec** as an argument never needs to do this:
 *
 * ```js
 * function operate(spec) {
 *   let blade;
 *   if (spec != null && spec.scalpel)
 *     blade = spec.scalpel;
 *   else
 *     blade = 10;
 * }
 * ```
 *
 * Instead, it can assume the spec is always present, and because **scalpel** is declared as required, it can assume
 * there is always a value.
 *
 * @see Result
 * @see Obj#validateObj
 *
 * @see Config
 * @see SeedData
 * @see Metadata
 */
abstract type Spec {

  afterMake: ~
}
